{"title":"Career Roadmap — Contracts Manager","role":"Contracts Manager","summary":"A Contracts Manager in construction manages the contractual and commercial side of projects: tendering, contract interpretation, procurement coordination, variations, claims, payment terms, extensions of time, subcontractor agreements, compliance, dispute avoidance and contract closeout.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High — Construction Engineering & Management is an excellent route because it combines civil/construction knowledge with project management and commercial-contract skills."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Civil/construction fundamentals, contracts, estimation, tendering, procurement and project documentation"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Contracts Engineer → Contract Administrator → Senior Contracts Engineer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Contracts Manager / Commercial Manager / Claims Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Commercial Manager, Contracts Head, Commercial Director or Project Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Civil fundamentals, engineering drawing, materials, communication, Excel"},{"text":"Understand construction projects and documentation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Construction technology, surveying, estimation, costing, quantity surveying"},{"text":"Prepare BOQs and basic tender documents"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Construction management, contracts, procurement, scheduling, claims"},{"text":"Analyse real/sample construction contracts"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Contract administration, FIDIC, variations, EOT, claims, dispute management"},{"text":"Complete a full simulated contract-management project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Construction Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Building materials"},{"text":"Construction methods"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Basic AutoCAD"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Technical communication"},{"text":"Construction terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Take a hypothetical residential project and create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Project scope"},{"text":"Work packages"},{"text":"Basic BOQ"},{"text":"Contractor responsibilities"},{"text":"Client responsibilities"},{"text":"Project deliverables"},{"text":"Preliminary payment structure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Estimation & Commercial Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quantity surveying"},{"text":"Quantity take-off"},{"text":"Estimation"},{"text":"Rate analysis"},{"text":"Construction costing"},{"text":"BOQ preparation"},{"text":"Tendering"},{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Construction scheduling"},{"text":"Basic accounting"},{"text":"Construction documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare a simulated tender package:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Tender Notice","Scope","BOQ","Technical Specifications","Commercial Terms","Bid Evaluation","Award Recommendation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Contracts Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contract types"},{"text":"Contract clauses"},{"text":"Scope interpretation"},{"text":"Employer/contractor obligations"},{"text":"Payment provisions"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Advance payments"},{"text":"Performance security"},{"text":"Variations"},{"text":"Extensions of time"},{"text":"Liquidated damages"},{"text":"Claims"},{"text":"Subcontract management"},{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Risk allocation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Contract Types"},{